# Everything that must NOT ship in the WordPress.org release package.
#
# The repository carries development history, test suites, program handoffs and
# validation artifacts. None of it runs at runtime, and shipping it is called out
# in the WordPress.org guidelines as a reason to reject a submission. The
# authoritative packager is scripts/build-release.sh, which copies an ALLOWLIST
# rather than trusting this file; this list exists so `wp dist-archive` and
# similar tools produce the same result.

# Version control / CI
.git
.gitignore
.github
.distignore
.deploy-exclude

# Development process: plans, handoffs, audits, validation output
.ai
.claude
docs
artifacts
tests
examples
scripts
build

# sdk/ is NOT excluded wholesale, and must not be.
#
# sdk/javascript/wpcc-mcp-relay.mjs is a runtime file. The configuration this
# plugin generates for Claude Desktop, Cursor, Codex and the rest tells the
# user's machine to fetch that exact path from their own site and run it (see
# Integration\BaseClientIntegration::relay_url()). Drop it and the fetch 404s,
# the connector never starts, and every connection fails silently.
#
# scripts/build-release.sh copies it explicitly and fails the build if it is
# missing. A bare `sdk` line here made this file disagree with the authoritative
# packager on the one file whose absence breaks the product, which defeats the
# purpose of keeping the two in step. Only the source-only samples are excluded.
sdk/php
sdk/javascript/client.js

# Root development documents
HANDOFF-STEP-*.md
PROJECT-HANDOFF-WPCC.md
WPCC-POST-STEP-101-ROADMAP.md
WPCC-RUNTIME-ROADMAP.md
*-REPORT.md
*-FINDING-*.md
STEP-*.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Developer tooling / local config
composer.json
composer.lock
vendor
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
phpcs.xml
phpcs.xml.dist
phpunit.xml
phpunit.xml.dist
wpcc-env.sh
wpcc-env*.sh
*.local.json
*.local.php

# API description used for development, not needed at runtime
openapi.json

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
